---
description: PointMe Project Implementation Guidelines
globs: ["**/*"]
alwaysApply: true
priority: 1
---

### Project Overview
PointMe is a Next.js application with TypeScript that provides a platform for connecting businesses with customers through location-based services. The application uses Supabase for backend services and follows a service-oriented architecture.

### Architectural Patterns
```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Service Layer] --> B[React Components]
    C[Hooks] --> B
    D[API Routes] --> A
    E[Toast Service] --> B
    F[Auth Service] --> B
```

### Code Standards
- Use PascalCase for component names (e.g., TextArea not Textarea)
- Use camelCase for variables, functions, and file names
- Prefer functional components with hooks over class components
- Implement proper type definitions (avoid 'any' types)
- Use index files for clean exports
- Follow singleton pattern for service implementations

### File Organization
- src/app: Next.js app router pages and layouts
- src/components: UI components and providers
- src/hooks: Custom React hooks
- src/lib: Core services and utilities
  - src/lib/core: Core functionality (auth, toast, etc.)
  - src/lib/supabase: Supabase client and services
- src/types: TypeScript type definitions
- src/constants: Application constants

### Critical Considerations
- Toast notifications use ToastService directly (e.g., ToastService.success, not ToastService.toast.success)
- Authentication uses centralized AuthService
- Error handling follows centralized pattern
- Component casing must be consistent (TextArea, not Textarea)
- Type safety is a priority (currently at 92% compliance)

### Active Issues
- Component casing standardization in progress
- Type assertions in transformers.ts need improvement
- Error handling centralization at 78% compliance
- Auth service duplication (high priority)

### Progress Tracking
- Update PROGRESS.md after each development session
- Update IMPLEMENTATION_ROADMAP.md for timeline changes
- Create session summaries in COMPOSER_SESSION_SUMMARY.md

### AI Assistance Guidelines
- Provide detailed context when requesting AI assistance
- Include file paths and expected outputs in queries
- Review and test AI-generated code thoroughly
- Document AI contributions in session summaries 